From f6b096ccfe918f4c8b0ae35444d52c4e94402339 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wilderness01 <140787484+Wilderness01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:08:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ultrawide: hook every calcMatrix vtable and follow the
 picture-shape setting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

V1.3.1 fills the screen but Mario is still ~22% fat: the vtable hook is installed and the trampoline runs, but it only ever saw a 4:3 projection — the main camera's projection does not go through CAM[1]'s vtable — and the direct-write fallback reads [CAM[0]], which holds the vtable address itself, not a projection object. The picture-shape setting is also ignored: UW only accepts aspects wider than 1.7866, so Duo (1.43), iPad (1.333) and 16:9 (0) all fall back to the display's 2.167, and Odyssey has no screen_aspect switch so the setting does not even appear for it.

Scan the module on the first present for every vtable whose calcMatrix slot holds sead::PerspectiveProjection::calcMatrix (main+0x9683c0) and hook each one, so the main camera is covered whichever vtable it uses; log every calcMatrix call by aspect (16:9 / 4:3 / other) with a 600-present summary, so the next log settles whether the main camera enters the hook; and make direct-write use the most recent trampoline-seen 16:9 projection object instead of the broken CAM[0] model (CAM[0]/CAM[2] are still parsed, but no longer pick the object). UW now follows DM_SCREEN_ASPECT: an explicit number is the target, wide or tall, 0 turns UW off without falling back to the display, and only auto/unset falls back to the display pixels; the present shape gains a taller branch (1920x(1920/a), a multiple of 48, as in loader.c). The settings add 1.333=iPad (4:3) to DM_SCREEN_ASPECT and screen_aspect on to Odyssey's profile, so the setting appears for the game.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The UW camera widening in 0098/0099/0101 never widened the main camera: the hook only covered CAM[1]'s vtable, which a 4:3 projection uses, while the main camera uses another vtable; the direct-write fallback read the vtable as an object; and UW ignored the picture-shape setting's explicit values. This patch hooks every calcMatrix vtable found by a first-frame scan, makes direct-write use a real trampoline-seen projection object, and makes UW follow DM_SCREEN_ASPECT (including the taller direction) with the iPad option added. No game patches are needed; the same DM_UW_* env as 0098 is required.
Issue: Wilderness01/NX2Apple#1
